A table renamed twice over two releases, `carte` to `menu` to `meal`, and
a database (a teammate's) that missed the first: the lines are followed
back, and it goes from `carte` to `meal` at once.

== before
CREATE TABLE carte (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO carte VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
-- @drop table carte
-- @from table menu = carte
-- @drop table menu
-- @from table meal = menu
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== query
SELECT id, title FROM meal

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `meal`: `carte` aside, to make it from
    ALTER TABLE "carte" RENAME TO "roux_old_carte"
  table `meal`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `meal`: its rows, by id, title
    INSERT INTO "meal" ("id", "title") SELECT "id", "title" FROM "roux_old_carte"
  table `meal`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_carte"

== rows
1 | lunch
